{
  "id": "L-009",
  "title": "The Precise Definition of a Limit",
  "atom_ids": ["A-09"],
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The informal definition from L-001 — 'arbitrarily close' — is a promise, not a definition: nothing in it says how close is close enough. The precise definition replaces the phrasing with a challenge game. It is the definition every limit so far has been working toward."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "definition",
      "term": "The epsilon-delta definition",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "We say "
        },
        { "type": "math", "source": "\\lim_{x \\to a} f(x) = L" },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " when: for every "
        },
        { "type": "math", "source": "\\varepsilon > 0" },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " there exists a "
        },
        { "type": "math", "source": "\\delta > 0" },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " such that whenever "
        },
        { "type": "math", "source": "0 < |x - a| < \\delta" },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ", we have "
        },
        { "type": "math", "source": "|f(x) - L| < \\varepsilon" },
        { "type": "text", "text": "." }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Read it as a game. Someone hands you an "
        },
        { "type": "math", "source": "\\varepsilon" },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " — how close the outputs must come to "
        },
        { "type": "math", "source": "L" },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ". You must hand back a "
        },
        { "type": "math", "source": "\\delta" },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " — how close the inputs must come to "
        },
        { "type": "math", "source": "a" },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " — that forces it. If you can answer every challenge, however small the "
        },
        { "type": "math", "source": "\\varepsilon" },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ", the limit is "
        },
        { "type": "math", "source": "L" },
        { "type": "text", "text": "." }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "widget",
      "name": "plot",
      "version": "1.0",
      "parameters": {
        "series": [
          {
            "label": "f(x) = 2x + 1",
            "points": [
              [0.5, 2.0], [0.7, 2.4], [0.9, 2.8], [1.0, 3.0],
              [1.1, 3.2], [1.3, 3.6], [1.5, 4.0]
            ]
          },
          {
            "label": "L + eps = 3.2",
            "points": [[0.7, 3.2], [1.3, 3.2]]
          },
          {
            "label": "L - eps = 2.8",
            "points": [[0.7, 2.8], [1.3, 2.8]]
          },
          {
            "label": "x = a - delta = 0.9",
            "points": [[0.9, 2.6], [0.9, 3.4]]
          },
          {
            "label": "x = a + delta = 1.1",
            "points": [[1.1, 2.6], [1.1, 3.4]]
          }
        ],
        "xlabel": "x",
        "ylabel": "y",
        "title": "The epsilon-delta window at a = 1, L = 3"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The window picture says it all: once "
        },
        { "type": "math", "source": "x" },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " lies strictly between "
        },
        { "type": "math", "source": "a - \\delta" },
        { "type": "text", "text": " and " },
        { "type": "math", "source": "a + \\delta" },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ", the graph of "
        },
        { "type": "math", "source": "f" },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " is trapped between "
        },
        { "type": "math", "source": "L - \\varepsilon" },
        { "type": "text", "text": " and " },
        { "type": "math", "source": "L + \\varepsilon" },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ". The smaller the "
        },
        { "type": "math", "source": "\\varepsilon" },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ", the narrower the window you must be able to guarantee — which is why "
        },
        { "type": "math", "source": "\\delta" },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " may depend on "
        },
        { "type": "math", "source": "\\varepsilon" },
        { "type": "text", "text": "." }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "equation",
      "source": "|(2x + 1) - 3| = |2x - 2| = 2|x - 1|",
      "display": true,
      "number": "(1)"
    },
    {
      "type": "worked-example",
      "title": "Proving a limit",
      "problem": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Prove that "
        },
        { "type": "math", "source": "\\lim_{x \\to 1} (2x + 1) = 3" },
        { "type": "text", "text": "." }
      ],
      "solution": [
        [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Let "
          },
          { "type": "math", "source": "\\varepsilon > 0" },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " be given. We must find "
          },
          { "type": "math", "source": "\\delta > 0" },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " such that "
          },
          { "type": "math", "source": "0 < |x - 1| < \\delta" },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " forces "
          },
          { "type": "math", "source": "|(2x + 1) - 3| < \\varepsilon" },
          { "type": "text", "text": "." }
        ],
        [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Simplify the target difference: "
          },
          { "type": "math", "source": "|(2x + 1) - 3| = 2|x - 1|" },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " (equation (1)). The distance from "
          },
          { "type": "math", "source": "f(x)" },
          { "type": "text", "text": " to " },
          { "type": "math", "source": "3" },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " is twice the distance from "
          },
          { "type": "math", "source": "x" },
          { "type": "text", "text": " to " },
          { "type": "math", "source": "1" },
          { "type": "text", "text": "." }
        ],
        [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Choose "
          },
          { "type": "math", "source": "\\delta = \\dfrac{\\varepsilon}{2}" },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ". Then whenever "
          },
          { "type": "math", "source": "0 < |x - 1| < \\delta" },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ", we get "
          },
          { "type": "math", "source": "|(2x + 1) - 3| = 2|x - 1| < 2\\delta = \\varepsilon" },
          { "type": "text", "text": "." }
        ],
        [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Every "
          },
          { "type": "math", "source": "\\varepsilon > 0" },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " is answered by the choice "
          },
          { "type": "math", "source": "\\delta = \\varepsilon/2" },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ", so the definition is satisfied and the limit is 3."
          }
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "The pattern is the whole technique: simplify the difference "
        },
        { "type": "math", "source": "|f(x) - L|" },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " until it is a constant times "
        },
        { "type": "math", "source": "|x - a|" },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ", then choose "
        },
        { "type": "math", "source": "\\delta" },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " small enough that the constant multiple stays under "
        },
        { "type": "math", "source": "\\varepsilon" },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ". And the '0 <' in the hypothesis keeps the definition silent about "
        },
        { "type": "math", "source": "f(a)" },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ": the limit never cares what happens at the point itself."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "callout",
      "kind": "important",
      "content": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "Every limit you computed in L-003 and L-004 rests on this definition. 'Just plug in' is the shortcut for the functions whose limits this definition proves exist. The epsilon-delta game is the ground truth the shortcuts stand on."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "formative",
      "prompt": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": "In the definition, the hypothesis on "
        },
        { "type": "math", "source": "x" },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": " is "
        },
        { "type": "math", "source": "0 < |x - a| < \\delta" },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ", not "
        },
        { "type": "math", "source": "|x - a| < \\delta" },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "text": ". What would change about the definition — and about which functions have limits — if the '0 <' were dropped?"
        }
      ],
      "kind": "free_response"
    }
  ]
}